# Secret Scan Allowlist
# One regex pattern per line. Lines matching these patterns are excluded from
# the pre-commit secret scan. These are known false positives in this codebase.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
# Patterns use grep -E (extended regex) syntax.

# --- Code reading environment variables (not actual secrets) ---
process\.env\.\w*(SECRET|PASSWORD|KEY|TOKEN|API_KEY)

# --- CLI command / tool definitions referencing secret-related operations ---
\.command\(.*secret
\.command\(.*password
\.description\(.*secret
\.description\(.*password
\.description\(.*[Kk]ey

# --- Code comments and prose that mention the words ---
//.*SECRET
//.*PASSWORD
//.*API.KEY
#.*SECRET
#.*PASSWORD
// .*password
// .*secret

# --- Documentation strings, help text, test assertions ---
secret scan
SECRET_SCAN
MCP_CU_SECRET_SCAN
SECRET_DETECTED
[Ss]ecret-scan
[Ss]ecret patterns?

# --- safety-service regex patterns (fake prefixes, not real secrets) ---
openai_anthropic_key
github_pat
aws_access_key
slack_bot_token

# --- tool descriptions + examples in src/ ---
rejects obvious secrets
Secrets \(sk-
Rejects obvious secrets

# --- this repo's audit + redaction docs ---
type_text secret
type_text.*reject
secrets .* base64

# --- Documentation of secret-scanning commands (grep example lines that
#     quote the scan regex). Applies to SKILL.md and any future docs.
grep -iE.*client_secret
grep -iE.*\(secret
grep -iE.*\(password
grep .*secret.*password.*(key|token)
